{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019APrpVsy8Bx5jzJT4cXHTm","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Plan: Batch fold_ple_from_evals Kernel Launches via Descriptor Array\n2\t\n3\t## Goal\n4\t\n5\tReplace the per-trace sequential `fold_ple_from_evals` GPU kernel launches in `LogupZerocheckGpu::fold_ple_evals` (mod.rs:1478-1594) with a single batched descriptor-array kernel. nsight shows `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<false>`: 797 instances, 9.5ms total at APC 300. The per-trace loop launches one kernel per matrix per trace, serializing on the GPU stream. A batched launch enables concurrent block scheduling across traces.\n6\t\n7\t## Current Code Path\n8\t\n9\t### Entry: `LogupZerocheckGpu::fold_ple_evals` (mod.rs:1478-1594)\n10\t\n11\tCalled once per segment at line 619, inside the Round 0 tracing span (after `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`, before MLE rounds begin). Runs on the default stream, single-threaded (NOT inside the multi-streamed section).\n12\t\n13\tThe function iterates all traces and launches `fold_ple_from_evals` per matrix:\n14\t\n15\t```rust\n16\tself.mat_evals_per_trace = ctx.per_trace.iter().map(|(air_idx, air_ctx)| {\n17\t    let mut results: Vec<DeviceMatrix<EF>> = Vec::new();\n18\t    // Preprocessed (if exists): fold_ple_evals_rotate → 1-2 kernel launches\n19\t    if let Some(committed) = &air_pk.preprocessed_data {\n20\t        results.push(fold_ple_evals_rotate(l_skip, ..., trace, ..., need_rot)?);\n21\t    }\n22\t    // Cached mains: fold_ple_evals_rotate → 1-2 launches each\n23\t    for committed in &air_ctx.cached_mains { ... }\n24\t    // Common main: fold_ple_evals_rotate → 1-2 launches\n25\t    results.push(fold_ple_evals_rotate(l_skip, ..., trace, ..., need_rot)?);\n26\t    Ok(results)\n27\t}).collect()?;\n28\t```\n29\t\n30\t### `fold_ple_evals_rotate` (fold_ple.rs:16-55)\n31\t\n32\tCalls `fold_ple_evals_gpu` once (rotate=false), and if `need_rot`, once more (rotate=true). Each call allocates a separate output `DeviceBuffer`, then launches the kernel.\n33\t\n34\t### `fold_ple_evals_gpu` → `fold_ple_from_evals` (fold_ple.rs:67-102)\n35\t\n36\tFFI call to `_fold_ple_from_evals` in `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`. Kernel: `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<ROTATE>`.\n37\t\n38\tGrid: `(ceil(num_x / chunks_per_block), width)`, block: `max(256, skip_domain)`.\n39\t\n40\tPer-thread: barycentric interpolation of `min(height, skip_domain)` source values into one output EF value. When `ROTATE=true`, source values are shifted by one position (modular rotation).\n41\t\n42\t### Parameters per launch\n43\t\n44\t- `src`: matrix data pointer (`*const F`)\n45\t- `dst`: output pointer (`*mut EF`)\n46\t- `omega_skip_pows`: shared across all traces\n47\t- `inv_lagrange_denoms`: shared across all traces\n48\t- `height`, `width`, `l_skip`, `num_x`: per-trace dimensions\n49\t- `rotate`: bool (template parameter)\n50\t\n51\t### Why it's slow at APC 300\n52\t\n53\t797 kernel launches at avg 12μs each = 9.5ms GPU time. Two costs:\n54\t1. **Kernel launch overhead**: ~2-3μs × 797 = ~2-2.4ms of CUDA driver overhead.\n55\t2. **Serial SM utilization**: Small traces (low width × low num_x) produce few blocks, leaving most of the 128 SMs idle while each small kernel runs to completion.\n56\t\n57\tAt APC 0: ~99 AIRs × ~1.3 matrices = ~130 launches across 5 segments, ~26 per segment. Savings proportionally smaller.\n58\t\n59\t## Changes\n60\t\n61\t### Step 1: Define descriptor struct (CUDA side)\n62\t\n63\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`\n64\t\n65\tFollow the existing `InterpColDesc` / `InterpTraceDescM` pattern in utils.cu (lines 77, 92) by embedding `block_start` directly in the descriptor:\n66\t\n67\t```c\n68\tstruct FoldPleDesc {\n69\t    const Fp *src;       // source matrix data pointer\n70\t    FpExt *dst;          // output buffer pointer (non-overlapping per trace)\n71\t    uint32_t height;     // source matrix height\n72\t    uint32_t width;      // source matrix width\n73\t    uint32_t num_x;      // = max(height, skip_domain) / skip_domain\n74\t    uint32_t block_start; // first 1D block index for this descriptor\n75\t};\n76\t```\n77\t\n78\t### Step 2: Add batched kernel using block_start + binary search\n79\t\n80\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`\n81\t\n82\tFollow the existing `batched_interpolate_columns_kernel` pattern in the same file (line 118):\n83\t\n84\t```c\n85\ttemplate <bool ROTATE>\n86\t__global__ void batched_fold_ple_from_evals_kernel(\n87\t    const FoldPleDesc *descs,\n88\t    uint32_t num_descs,\n89\t    const Fp *omega_skip_pows,\n90\t    const FpExt *inv_lagrange_denoms,\n91\t    uint32_t skip_domain\n92\t) {\n93\t    // Binary search on block_start to find descriptor for this block\n94\t    uint32_t lo = 0, hi = num_descs;\n95\t    while (lo < hi) {\n96\t        uint32_t mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n97\t        if (descs[mid].block_start <= blockIdx.x) lo = mid + 1;\n98\t        else hi = mid;\n99\t    }\n100\t    uint32_t desc_idx = lo - 1;\n101\t    auto desc = descs[desc_idx];\n102\t    uint32_t local_block = blockIdx.x - desc.block_start;\n103\t\n104\t    // Decompose local_block into (row_block, col_idx) using desc dimensions\n105\t    uint32_t chunks_per_block = blockDim.x / skip_domain;\n106\t    uint32_t blocks_per_col = (desc.num_x + chunks_per_block - 1) / chunks_per_block;\n107\t    uint32_t col_idx = local_block / blocks_per_col;\n108\t    uint32_t row_block = local_block % blocks_per_col;\n109\t\n110\t    // Same body as existing fold_ple_from_evals_kernel:\n111\t    // - chunk_in_block = threadIdx.x / skip_domain\n112\t    // - tid_in_chunk = threadIdx.x % skip_domain\n113\t    // - row_idx = row_block * chunks_per_block + chunk_in_block\n114\t    // - Barycentric interpolation from desc.src → writes to desc.dst\n115\t}\n116\t```\n117\t\n118\t### Step 3: Add C launcher\n119\t\n120\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`\n121\t\n122\t```c\n123\textern \"C\" int _batched_fold_ple_from_evals(\n124\t    const FoldPleDesc *descs,\n125\t    uint32_t num_descs,\n126\t    uint32_t total_blocks,\n127\t    const Fp *omega_skip_pows,\n128\t    const FpExt *inv_lagrange_denoms,\n129\t    uint32_t l_skip,\n130\t    bool rotate\n131\t) {\n132\t    if (total_blocks == 0) return 0;\n133\t    uint32_t skip_domain = 1u << l_skip;\n134\t    uint32_t block_size = std::max(256u, skip_domain);\n135\t    size_t smem = (skip_domain > WARP_SIZE) ?\n136\t        (block_size / WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt) : 0;\n137\t    \n138\t    if (rotate) {\n139\t        batched_fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<true><<<total_blocks, block_size, smem>>>(\n140\t            descs, num_descs, omega_skip_pows, inv_lagrange_denoms, skip_domain);\n141\t    } else {\n142\t        batched_fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<false><<<total_blocks, block_size, smem>>>(\n143\t            descs, num_descs, omega_skip_pows, inv_lagrange_denoms, skip_domain);\n144\t    }\n145\t    return CHECK_KERNEL();\n146\t}\n147\t```\n148\t\n149\t### Step 4: Add Rust FFI bindings\n150\t\n151\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n152\t\n153\tAdd `#[repr(C)]` struct `FoldPleDesc` and the extern \"C\" + safe wrapper for `batched_fold_ple_from_evals`.\n154\t\n155\t### Step 5: Add batched dispatch function in fold_ple.rs\n156\t\n157\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fold_ple.rs`\n158\t\n159\tAdd a new function that batches the kernel launches but keeps per-trace output allocation:\n160\t\n161\t```rust\n162\t/// Batch-launches fold_ple_from_evals for multiple (src, dst) pairs.\n163\t/// Each pair gets its own output range; the kernel processes all pairs concurrently.\n164\tpub unsafe fn batched_fold_ple_evals_gpu(\n165\t    l_skip: usize,\n166\t    d_omega_skip_pows: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n167\t    items: &[(/*src*/ &DeviceBuffer<F>, /*src_height*/ usize, /*src_width*/ usize,\n168\t              /*dst*/ *mut EF, /*num_x*/ usize)],\n169\t    d_inv_lagrange_denoms: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n170\t    rotate: bool,\n171\t) -> Result<(), FoldPleError>\n172\t```\n173\t\n174\tThis function:\n175\t1. Builds `Vec<FoldPleDesc>` from the `items` slice, computing `block_start` as cumulative block count.\n176\t2. Uploads the descriptor array to device.\n177\t3. Calls `batched_fold_ple_from_evals` with `total_blocks = last.block_start + last_blocks`.\n178\t4. For 0 items, returns immediately.\n179\t\n180\tThen modify `fold_ple_evals_rotate` to collect its 1-2 fold calls into a batch rather than launching individually. This keeps the mod.rs per-trace loop structure and mem_limit accounting completely unchanged.\n181\t\n182\t### Step 6: Wire fold_ple_evals_rotate to use batched path\n183\t\n184\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fold_ple.rs`\n185\t\n186\tModify `fold_ple_evals_rotate` (or add a new `batched_fold_ple_evals_rotate` that takes multiple traces) to collect all the (src, dst, height, width, num_x) tuples and call `batched_fold_ple_evals_gpu` twice: once for rotate=false (all traces), once for rotate=true (traces with need_rot).\n187\t\n188\tIn mod.rs `fold_ple_evals`, collect all the trace matrix information in a first pass, then call the batch function(s), then distribute the results. The per-trace output `DeviceBuffer` allocation and `DeviceMatrix` construction remain in fold_ple.rs. The `mem_limit` accounting at line 1533 applies to the same per-trace buffer and is unchanged.\n189\t\n190\t## Invariants\n191\t\n192\t1. **Output equivalence**: Identical computation per block. The descriptor provides per-trace parameters.\n193\t2. **Destination non-overlap**: Each descriptor's `dst` points to a separately allocated `DeviceBuffer`.\n194\t3. **Shared parameters**: `omega_skip_pows`, `inv_lagrange_denoms`, `skip_domain` are the same for all traces.\n195\t4. **Block size**: Same as existing: `max(256, skip_domain)`. Shared memory allocation unchanged.\n196\t5. **Per-trace output allocation preserved**: Downstream `mat_evals_per_trace` receives the same per-trace `DeviceMatrix` types.\n197\t6. **Height=0 or width=0 traces**: Filtered out during descriptor building (matching fold_ple.rs:78-80).\n198\t7. **save_memory accounting**: `mem_limit` subtraction for common_main (line 1533) uses per-trace buffer sizes — unchanged since per-trace allocation is preserved.\n199\t\n200\t## Measurement Plan\n201\t\n202\t1. Run benchmarks for APC {0, 100, 300}.\n203\t2. Primary metric: Round 0 at APC 300 — expect ~3-5ms reduction (181ms → 176-178ms) from faster fold_ple_evals.\n204\t3. STARK excl trace at APC 300 — expect same ~3-5ms reduction (1129ms → 1124-1126ms).\n205\t4. APC 0: expect no regression (batched path active with ~26 per-segment launches, overhead negligible).\n206\t5. nsight: `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<false>` instances should drop from ~797 to ~2-4.\n207\t\n208\t## Rollback Criteria\n209\t\n210\t- Round 0 improvement at APC 300 < 3ms\n211\t- APC 0 regression > 5ms on STARK excl trace\n212\t- Correctness failure at any APC config\n213\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ad7abbbb-1391-43dc-94f8-6f027601bba7","uuid":"073a916a-8026-42b5-b584-64adb04fdb61","timestamp":"2026-04-16T00:25:07.532Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-16-0200-batch-fold-ple-descriptor-array/plan.md","content":"# Plan: Batch fold_ple_from_evals Kernel Launches via Descriptor Array\n\n## Goal\n\nReplace the per-trace sequential `fold_ple_from_evals` GPU kernel launches in `LogupZerocheckGpu::fold_ple_evals` (mod.rs:1478-1594) with a single batched descriptor-array kernel. nsight shows `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<false>`: 797 instances, 9.5ms total at APC 300. The per-trace loop launches one kernel per matrix per trace, serializing on the GPU stream. A batched launch enables concurrent block scheduling across traces.\n\n## Current Code Path\n\n### Entry: `LogupZerocheckGpu::fold_ple_evals` (mod.rs:1478-1594)\n\nCalled once per segment at line 619, inside the Round 0 tracing span (after `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`, before MLE rounds begin). Runs on the default stream, single-threaded (NOT inside the multi-streamed section).\n\nThe function iterates all traces and launches `fold_ple_from_evals` per matrix:\n\n```rust\nself.mat_evals_per_trace = ctx.per_trace.iter().map(|(air_idx, air_ctx)| {\n    let mut results: Vec<DeviceMatrix<EF>> = Vec::new();\n    // Preprocessed (if exists): fold_ple_evals_rotate → 1-2 kernel launches\n    if let Some(committed) = &air_pk.preprocessed_data {\n        results.push(fold_ple_evals_rotate(l_skip, ..., trace, ..., need_rot)?);\n    }\n    // Cached mains: fold_ple_evals_rotate → 1-2 launches each\n    for committed in &air_ctx.cached_mains { ... }\n    // Common main: fold_ple_evals_rotate → 1-2 launches\n    results.push(fold_ple_evals_rotate(l_skip, ..., trace, ..., need_rot)?);\n    Ok(results)\n}).collect()?;\n```\n\n### `fold_ple_evals_rotate` (fold_ple.rs:16-55)\n\nCalls `fold_ple_evals_gpu` once (rotate=false), and if `need_rot`, once more (rotate=true). Each call allocates a separate output `DeviceBuffer`, then launches the kernel.\n\n### `fold_ple_evals_gpu` → `fold_ple_from_evals` (fold_ple.rs:67-102)\n\nFFI call to `_fold_ple_from_evals` in `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`. Kernel: `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<ROTATE>`.\n\nGrid: `(ceil(num_x / chunks_per_block), width)`, block: `max(256, skip_domain)`.\n\nPer-thread: barycentric interpolation of `min(height, skip_domain)` source values into one output EF value. When `ROTATE=true`, source values are shifted by one position (modular rotation).\n\n### Parameters per launch\n\n- `src`: matrix data pointer (`*const F`)\n- `dst`: output pointer (`*mut EF`)\n- `omega_skip_pows`: shared across all traces\n- `inv_lagrange_denoms`: shared across all traces\n- `height`, `width`, `l_skip`, `num_x`: per-trace dimensions\n- `rotate`: bool (template parameter)\n\n### Why it's slow at APC 300\n\n797 kernel launches at avg 12μs each = 9.5ms GPU time. Two costs:\n1. **Kernel launch overhead**: ~2-3μs × 797 = ~2-2.4ms of CUDA driver overhead.\n2. **Serial SM utilization**: Small traces (low width × low num_x) produce few blocks, leaving most of the 128 SMs idle while each small kernel runs to completion.\n\nAt APC 0: ~99 AIRs × ~1.3 matrices = ~130 launches across 5 segments, ~26 per segment. Savings proportionally smaller.\n\n## Changes\n\n### Step 1: Define descriptor struct (CUDA side)\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`\n\nFollow the existing `InterpColDesc` / `InterpTraceDescM` pattern in utils.cu (lines 77, 92) by embedding `block_start` directly in the descriptor:\n\n```c\nstruct FoldPleDesc {\n    const Fp *src;       // source matrix data pointer\n    FpExt *dst;          // output buffer pointer (non-overlapping per trace)\n    uint32_t height;     // source matrix height\n    uint32_t width;      // source matrix width\n    uint32_t num_x;      // = max(height, skip_domain) / skip_domain\n    uint32_t block_start; // first 1D block index for this descriptor\n};\n```\n\n### Step 2: Add batched kernel using block_start + binary search\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`\n\nFollow the existing `batched_interpolate_columns_kernel` pattern in the same file (line 118):\n\n```c\ntemplate <bool ROTATE>\n__global__ void batched_fold_ple_from_evals_kernel(\n    const FoldPleDesc *descs,\n    uint32_t num_descs,\n    const Fp *omega_skip_pows,\n    const FpExt *inv_lagrange_denoms,\n    uint32_t skip_domain\n) {\n    // Binary search on block_start to find descriptor for this block\n    uint32_t lo = 0, hi = num_descs;\n    while (lo < hi) {\n        uint32_t mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n        if (descs[mid].block_start <= blockIdx.x) lo = mid + 1;\n        else hi = mid;\n    }\n    uint32_t desc_idx = lo - 1;\n    auto desc = descs[desc_idx];\n    uint32_t local_block = blockIdx.x - desc.block_start;\n\n    // Decompose local_block into (row_block, col_idx) using desc dimensions\n    uint32_t chunks_per_block = blockDim.x / skip_domain;\n    uint32_t blocks_per_col = (desc.num_x + chunks_per_block - 1) / chunks_per_block;\n    uint32_t col_idx = local_block / blocks_per_col;\n    uint32_t row_block = local_block % blocks_per_col;\n\n    // Same body as existing fold_ple_from_evals_kernel:\n    // - chunk_in_block = threadIdx.x / skip_domain\n    // - tid_in_chunk = threadIdx.x % skip_domain\n    // - row_idx = row_block * chunks_per_block + chunk_in_block\n    // - Barycentric interpolation from desc.src → writes to desc.dst\n}\n```\n\n### Step 3: Add C launcher\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/utils.cu`\n\n```c\nextern \"C\" int _batched_fold_ple_from_evals(\n    const FoldPleDesc *descs,\n    uint32_t num_descs,\n    uint32_t total_blocks,\n    const Fp *omega_skip_pows,\n    const FpExt *inv_lagrange_denoms,\n    uint32_t l_skip,\n    bool rotate\n) {\n    if (total_blocks == 0) return 0;\n    uint32_t skip_domain = 1u << l_skip;\n    uint32_t block_size = std::max(256u, skip_domain);\n    size_t smem = (skip_domain > WARP_SIZE) ?\n        (block_size / WARP_SIZE) * sizeof(FpExt) : 0;\n    \n    if (rotate) {\n        batched_fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<true><<<total_blocks, block_size, smem>>>(\n            descs, num_descs, omega_skip_pows, inv_lagrange_denoms, skip_domain);\n    } else {\n        batched_fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<false><<<total_blocks, block_size, smem>>>(\n            descs, num_descs, omega_skip_pows, inv_lagrange_denoms, skip_domain);\n    }\n    return CHECK_KERNEL();\n}\n```\n\n### Step 4: Add Rust FFI bindings\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs`\n\nAdd `#[repr(C)]` struct `FoldPleDesc` and the extern \"C\" + safe wrapper for `batched_fold_ple_from_evals`.\n\n### Step 5: Add batched dispatch function in fold_ple.rs\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fold_ple.rs`\n\nAdd a new function that batches the kernel launches but keeps per-trace output allocation:\n\n```rust\n/// Batch-launches fold_ple_from_evals for multiple (src, dst) pairs.\n/// Each pair gets its own output range; the kernel processes all pairs concurrently.\npub unsafe fn batched_fold_ple_evals_gpu(\n    l_skip: usize,\n    d_omega_skip_pows: &DeviceBuffer<F>,\n    items: &[(/*src*/ &DeviceBuffer<F>, /*src_height*/ usize, /*src_width*/ usize,\n              /*dst*/ *mut EF, /*num_x*/ usize)],\n    d_inv_lagrange_denoms: &DeviceBuffer<EF>,\n    rotate: bool,\n) -> Result<(), FoldPleError>\n```\n\nThis function:\n1. Builds `Vec<FoldPleDesc>` from the `items` slice, computing `block_start` as cumulative block count.\n2. Uploads the descriptor array to device.\n3. Calls `batched_fold_ple_from_evals` with `total_blocks = last.block_start + last_blocks`.\n4. For 0 items, returns immediately.\n\nThen modify `fold_ple_evals_rotate` to collect its 1-2 fold calls into a batch rather than launching individually. This keeps the mod.rs per-trace loop structure and mem_limit accounting completely unchanged.\n\n### Step 6: Wire fold_ple_evals_rotate to use batched path\n\n**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/fold_ple.rs`\n\nModify `fold_ple_evals_rotate` (or add a new `batched_fold_ple_evals_rotate` that takes multiple traces) to collect all the (src, dst, height, width, num_x) tuples and call `batched_fold_ple_evals_gpu` twice: once for rotate=false (all traces), once for rotate=true (traces with need_rot).\n\nIn mod.rs `fold_ple_evals`, collect all the trace matrix information in a first pass, then call the batch function(s), then distribute the results. The per-trace output `DeviceBuffer` allocation and `DeviceMatrix` construction remain in fold_ple.rs. The `mem_limit` accounting at line 1533 applies to the same per-trace buffer and is unchanged.\n\n## Invariants\n\n1. **Output equivalence**: Identical computation per block. The descriptor provides per-trace parameters.\n2. **Destination non-overlap**: Each descriptor's `dst` points to a separately allocated `DeviceBuffer`.\n3. **Shared parameters**: `omega_skip_pows`, `inv_lagrange_denoms`, `skip_domain` are the same for all traces.\n4. **Block size**: Same as existing: `max(256, skip_domain)`. Shared memory allocation unchanged.\n5. **Per-trace output allocation preserved**: Downstream `mat_evals_per_trace` receives the same per-trace `DeviceMatrix` types.\n6. **Height=0 or width=0 traces**: Filtered out during descriptor building (matching fold_ple.rs:78-80).\n7. **save_memory accounting**: `mem_limit` subtraction for common_main (line 1533) uses per-trace buffer sizes — unchanged since per-trace allocation is preserved.\n\n## Measurement Plan\n\n1. Run benchmarks for APC {0, 100, 300}.\n2. Primary metric: Round 0 at APC 300 — expect ~3-5ms reduction (181ms → 176-178ms) from faster fold_ple_evals.\n3. STARK excl trace at APC 300 — expect same ~3-5ms reduction (1129ms → 1124-1126ms).\n4. APC 0: expect no regression (batched path active with ~26 per-segment launches, overhead negligible).\n5. nsight: `fold_ple_from_evals_kernel<false>` instances should drop from ~797 to ~2-4.\n\n## Rollback Criteria\n\n- Round 0 improvement at APC 300 < 3ms\n- APC 0 regression > 5ms on STARK excl trace\n- Correctness failure at any APC config\n","numLines":213,"startLine":1,"totalLines":213}}}
